notes.body:
Many writes in this app use one pattern, often called *compare-and-set*. Instead of "read the row, decide, then update it by id", the update itself carries the conditions the decision relied on: `updateMany({ where: { id, someField: expectedValue }, data: {...} })`. The database checks the `where` at the moment of writing and reports how many rows it changed (`count`).

The concepts guide shows three such predicates side by side and suggests reading each as a sentence. Before the quizzes, find all three in `src/repositories/ticketRepository.ts` and, for each one:

- write its `where` as a sentence, and say what has to be true about the row for the write to happen;
- work out what happens if two requests run it for the same row at the same moment;
- follow the caller and note what it does when it gets back `null` (zero rows), including whether it writes an audit row.
